1
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:19,670
...Brother... amazing as always.

2
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:24,050
...Brother... truly amazing.

3
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:30,110
How do you feel, with the world's eyes on you as a genius football child, Itoshi Sae-kun?

4
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:33,340
What kind of player do you want to become in the future?

5
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:36,370
Shut up, it's none of your business, it's my own concern.

6
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:37,720
...Ah!

7
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:39,200
Let's go home, Rin.

8
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:40,470
Okay.

9
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:43,940
H-He already has a star aura!

10
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:49,610
A-And now, let's return to our program! Here's footage of the incredible performance Sae-kun delivered!

11
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:53,570
...Brother... is a bit funny.

12
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:59,990
I won! What about you, brother?

13
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,350
Someone who wastes their luck on such things will never become the best in the world.

14
00:01:08,730 --> 00:01:11,420
Really? Is that how luck works?

15
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:14,430
I will become the world's best striker.

16
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:16,500
...And nothing else has any value to me.

17
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:22,480
...Brother... hates losing.

18
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:29,710
Far side! Far side!

19
00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:31,520
Mark Itoshi Sae!

20
00:01:32,170 --> 00:01:34,490
...Brother... never loses to anyone.

21
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:37,430
...And I.

22
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:43,160
...I want to, too.

23
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:48,000
...I want to become strong and amazing, just like my brother!

24
00:01:58,610 --> 00:01:59,300
Rin!

25
00:02:03,370 --> 00:02:06,770
Can I... become the world's best striker too...?

26
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:14,360
Hey! Who's this pipsqueak?

27
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:15,450
Move!

28
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:18,490
...Sorry, brother, I...

29
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,180
That was amazing, Rin!

30
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:24,200
Play football with me!

31
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:30,500
You're the only one who can become the best after me!

32
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:32,390
Okay.

33
00:02:33,450 --> 00:02:37,130
Brother... is the kindest person in the world.

34
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,650
Isn't this amazing, darling?

35
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:21,400
...Even just Yu-chan being selected as a starter is incredible...

36
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:22,990
...and his team is even in the lead!

37
00:04:23,210 --> 00:04:27,320
I'm so happy even though I don't understand a thing about football!

38
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:31,310
What are you doing, Meguru?!

39
00:04:31,310 --> 00:04:33,540
You have to try harder to score!

40
00:04:33,630 --> 00:04:36,250
Can you even call yourself a forward like that?!

41
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:40,560
Whoa! I'm sorry! My son is playing, so I got carried away!

42
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:43,130
Oh! Our son is too!

43
00:04:43,130 --> 00:04:45,050
He's number 11!

44
00:04:45,050 --> 00:04:48,800
Really?! And on the same team?! My son is number 8!

45
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:50,630
This is so amazing!

46
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,600
Shake hands, shake hands!

47
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:56,230
Thank you so much for having your son play with mine!

48
00:04:57,210 --> 00:05:00,190
...I feel like I'm seeing him for the first time.

49
00:05:02,250 --> 00:05:05,110
Enjoying playing like this!

50
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,690
It's our pleasure!

51
00:05:07,690 --> 00:05:10,830
Thank you for your support!

52
00:05:11,190 --> 00:05:12,340
Hyoma!

53
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:15,340
Here, here! Hyoma!

54
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,750
He saw us, Mom!

55
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:21,520
Hey, you! Who's that beauty?

56
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:22,570
...My older sister.

57
00:05:22,570 --> 00:05:25,020
...That's not ordinary...! What striking siblings you two are!

58
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:26,800
Aaah, so embarrassing!

59
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:30,800
Hyoma's face has the same expression he had back then.

60
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:34,450
...Yes... he's finally back to his old self.

61
00:05:35,930 --> 00:05:38,810
What's the meaning of this, Coach?!

62
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:42,960
Don't you know why we arranged this match?

63
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:47,610
O-Of course I know.

64
00:05:47,610 --> 00:05:52,580
...But contrary to our expectations, th-the opponent...

65
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:56,600
The victor represents justice, and the loser represents evil.

66
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,920
I don't want excuses.

67
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:07,050
...I don't care how you do it, Hoi-chan.

68
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:13,600
You must win today to represent the justice of Japanese football!!!

69
00:06:15,910 --> 00:06:18,880
Results are all that matter in the world of sports.

70
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:21,720
Crush Blue Lock!

71
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,320
Yessss!!!

72
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:27,490
We can win!! We're amazing!

73
00:06:27,490 --> 00:06:28,880
...Did you see?

74
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:33,310
My glamorous clearance of that certain goal?

75
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,590
Get your leg out of my face!

76
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:40,000
That was an amazing run, Chigiri-kun.

77
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:41,500
Is your leg okay?

78
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:43,320
Thank you, Hiori!

79
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:45,850
Yes, I can still run!

80
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,170
...Towel... towel.

81
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:51,980
...Here, Nagi.

82
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,470
...Your goal was amazing.

83
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:55,790
But you can score more, right...?

84
00:06:56,270 --> 00:06:57,470
...I know you can.

85
00:06:57,770 --> 00:06:58,910
...Yeah, Reo.

86
00:06:59,530 --> 00:07:00,740
...I can score more.

87
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:06,360
Congratulations to all of you on your first half performance!

88
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,930
Thanks!

89
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:11,200
Calm down, you unpolished gems.

90
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:13,830
First, let's summarize the first half.

91
00:07:13,830 --> 00:07:16,300
Why were you able to score?

92
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:20,680
You need to engrave the details of what's happened so far into your minds.

93
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:24,710
...We entered this match with a game plan.

94
00:07:24,710 --> 00:07:27,690
But it didn't work at first.

95
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:32,220
...And it was Itoshi Rin who broke that first.

96
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,980
With the help of Isagi Yoichi.

97
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:37,940
...By shortening the passing distance.

98
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:40,550
...And by keeping Isagi Yoichi within your range at all times.

99
00:07:40,550 --> 00:07:43,480
...You expanded your options even further.

100
00:07:44,110 --> 00:07:47,020
Why did you do that, Itoshi Rin?

101
00:07:47,450 --> 00:07:52,250
To break through their back four... I needed a scapegoat.

102
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,160
Isagi just happened to be near me, that's all.

103
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:56,870
...A scapegoat, then.

104
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,580
I liked your answer.

105
00:07:59,030 --> 00:08:01,620
...Something like that isn't produced by training.

106
00:08:02,070 --> 00:08:06,590
So, Isagi Yoichi, do you consider yourself a scapegoat?

107
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,670
Absolutely not! I intend to score as well!

108
00:08:09,670 --> 00:08:12,130
...Exactly... that's what's required.

109
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:15,350
...In every single one of you standing on that pitch...

110
00:08:15,350 --> 00:08:20,560
...you have the egoism needed to believe you are the heroes of this match and fight to the bitter end.

111
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:24,570
And that is what allowed us to take the lead in the first half.

112
00:08:24,970 --> 00:08:28,730
But there's no guarantee the second half will go the same way.

113
00:08:28,730 --> 00:08:31,420
In fact... it's almost impossible.

114
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:35,860
So let's stop this premature celebration.

115
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,920
You haven't accomplished anything yet!

116
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:44,080
Don't settle for this! Keep attacking!

117
00:08:44,490 --> 00:08:49,180
And let each and every one of you refuse to give up your right to become the hero of this match until the very last second!

118
00:08:50,010 --> 00:08:50,830
That's all.

119
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:53,130
We won't make any substitutions.

120
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:57,260
...I have one instruction for you for the second half.

121
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,500
Crush them.

122
00:09:01,130 --> 00:09:02,260
...That's right.

123
00:09:02,650 --> 00:09:06,560
...We're not playing for the sake of winning together.

124
00:09:07,130 --> 00:09:09,540
...I need to strive harder for my own goal.

125
00:09:10,030 --> 00:09:12,780
...Just like he does in his own way!

126
00:09:13,910 --> 00:09:17,120
I'm going to prove myself in this match!

127
00:09:18,490 --> 00:09:21,940
What a disaster... What a disaster... What a disasterrr!

128
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:24,200
...I never thought they'd turn the score around.

129
00:09:24,530 --> 00:09:26,540
What are we going to do in the second half?

130
00:09:27,130 --> 00:09:28,920
...If only I had scored.

131
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:32,250
You came just in time, genius!

132
00:09:32,250 --> 00:09:34,510
We're discussing what to do in the second half.

133
00:09:34,510 --> 00:09:37,760
Our last attack in the half was effective.

134
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:40,300
They might get rattled if we increase our numbers in attack more!

135
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:42,850
Should we ask the coach to change the formation?

136
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:45,240
Do whatever you want.

137
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,730
This is no longer my concern.

138
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:49,440
What are you saying?!

139
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:52,890
I'm leaving.

140
00:09:54,530 --> 00:09:55,850
What do you mean?

141
00:09:55,850 --> 00:09:58,250
The match can't go on without you!

142
00:09:58,250 --> 00:10:00,030
...He's washing his face.

143
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:04,630
Like I care. I just accepted that stupid bet of your captain.

144
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:07,080
A bet with Aiku...?

145
00:10:07,130 --> 00:10:10,130
Win for us without using Shidou.

146
00:10:10,170 --> 00:10:12,590
I'm the one testing you, not the other way around.

147
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:16,640
And if you can't keep up with me, I'll leave the match immediately.

148
00:10:17,650 --> 00:10:20,820
And it turns out you're a bunch of useless scrap.

149
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:22,430
That's the reality.

150
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:27,460
...Anyway... I only came because Blue Lock caught my interest.

151
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:31,020
...They may lack experience.

152
00:10:31,020 --> 00:10:35,120
But the world they see, and the place they aspire to reach, are completely different from yours.

153
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:39,130
And knowing that is more than enough for me.

154
00:10:40,370 --> 00:10:42,870
There's no longer any reason for me to stay here any longer.

155
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,210
Hold on a moment, little genius!

156
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:51,230
...I'm sorry for making that selfish bet, guys.

157
00:10:51,990 --> 00:10:55,670
...I wanted to test our current strength.

158
00:10:56,520 --> 00:11:00,380
...And see how far we've come.

159
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:03,560
...But now I'm sure.

160
00:11:04,410 --> 00:11:05,390
...We're...

161
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,620
...weak.

162
00:11:11,050 --> 00:11:17,900
And at this rate, the ones who will be stripped of their right to represent the U-20s and disappear... are us.

163
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:25,150
...I've never felt such a burning pain since the day I was born.

164
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:28,300
It's too late to realize that now.

165
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:31,460
If I leave, any hope you have of winning disappears.

166
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:34,210
...But we still have a chance.

167
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:36,980
We still have that demon!

168
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:40,030
Genius!

169
00:11:40,030 --> 00:11:44,640
Isn't having a creature like me on the team reason enough to keep fighting?

170
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:48,550
...So that was your aim from the very beginning.

171
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,710
Wreak havoc for me, you demon.

172
00:11:55,290 --> 00:11:58,400
You and I will be the stars of this big stage!

173
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,540
...If you remain fixated on being my little brother,

174
00:12:15,510 --> 00:12:19,180
you'll never surpass me... as long as I live.

175
00:12:20,170 --> 00:12:22,730
...Just watch me, you filthy brother.

176
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:25,300
...Because I...

177
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:33,060
My dream is to become a footballer just like my brother.

178
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:36,020
...And my brother will become the world's best striker.

179
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:41,810
And I'll be the world's second-best striker... and together we'll win the World Cup.

180
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:44,490
...The Itoshi brothers are so terrifying!

181
00:12:44,490 --> 00:12:46,030
They're monsters!

182
00:12:46,030 --> 00:12:48,550
You were too lax on your last shot, Rin!

183
00:12:48,550 --> 00:12:50,740
Really? I'll be more careful on the next one.

184
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:53,750
Can you raise your speed a bit more?

185
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:56,210
Of course. I'll try.

186
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:59,670
...Playing football with my brother is fun.

187
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:03,130
...When I play with my brother... I was invincible!

188
00:13:05,330 --> 00:13:07,550
I'll become the best in the world alongside my brother!

189
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,760
Yessss!

190
00:13:13,430 --> 00:13:14,560
...I won again.

191
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:17,000
You're wasting your luck on trivial things, Rin.

192
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:20,650
...I'll destroy the evidence.

193
00:13:22,870 --> 00:13:26,890
Rin... what do you think about while you're playing football?

194
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:29,120
...Nothing in particular.

195
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:31,840
I guess I'm just thinking about scoring.

196
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:35,830
And I know that if I run into the danger zones, your passes will reach me.

197
00:13:36,330 --> 00:13:38,000
What do you mean by danger zones?

198
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:42,960
...Those areas where the opponent panics and collapses.

199
00:13:45,690 --> 00:13:48,830
You rely too much on your instincts.

200
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:51,930
But you still pass to me anyway, so what's the problem?

201
00:13:51,930 --> 00:13:54,890
...Honestly, playing with others doesn't satisfy me.

202
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:58,600
And what do you intend to do when I'm no longer here?

203
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:02,190
...Honestly, I don't know... but I guess I'd look for someone to replace you.

204
00:14:02,190 --> 00:14:04,530
...As if someone could!

205
00:14:04,530 --> 00:14:06,200
Who do you think you're talking to?!

206
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,070
...Agh!

207
00:14:07,330 --> 00:14:12,030
Okay, okay, I get it...! Itoshi Sae-sama, the best in the world!

208
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:16,840
I'm leaving for Spain tomorrow, Rin.

209
00:14:17,260 --> 00:14:21,380
...To join the youth team of Real Madrid, the best team in the world.

210
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,750
Why did you suddenly turn serious?

211
00:14:24,070 --> 00:14:25,090
...I already know that.

212
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:28,800
Aren't you going to become the best striker in the world, brother?

213
00:14:29,130 --> 00:14:32,430
I'm one step ahead of you... so hurry up and catch up to me!

214
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:36,980
And while I'm gone... don't you dare give up!

215
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,460
...Got it.

216
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:43,440
...For now, I'll aim to become the best in Japan to attract the attention of scouts like you.

217
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:45,890
Exactly...! And then aim for the world!

218
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,740
We'll both become the best in the world!

219
00:14:51,610 --> 00:14:53,580
...Honestly, I was a little sad, but...

220
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:56,170
...I'll definitely catch up to him!

221
00:14:56,830 --> 00:14:58,790
Take care, brother.

222
00:14:59,030 --> 00:15:00,370
I'm off!

223
00:15:00,370 --> 00:15:02,790
To become the world's best striker!

224
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:07,610
...When I meet him again... I want to be...

225
00:15:09,210 --> 00:15:12,180
...a player who can fight on the world's stages!

226
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:16,890
...Playing football without my brother feels restricted and uncomfortable, but...

227
00:15:16,890 --> 00:15:18,100
Pass it, Rin!

228
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:18,890
Over here, Rin!

229
00:15:18,890 --> 00:15:19,770
Pass the ball to me!

230
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,990
...To get even a little closer to my brother...

231
00:15:23,710 --> 00:15:25,940
...I have to lead this team he left behind.

232
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:31,780
...To become the best in Japan in his place!

233
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:36,800
Good work! Are you staying to train today too?

234
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:37,530
Yeah.

235
00:15:37,530 --> 00:15:40,170
It's so cold! I'm heading out before you, Rin!

236
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:49,110
...Snow.

237
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:54,340
Wasn't that shot easy to save?

238
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,430
...Bro-

239
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:03,620
...Welcome back.

240
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:06,840
...Yeah... I'm back.

241
00:16:08,330 --> 00:16:10,170
...I was always following your news!

242
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:13,860
...You played in matches for the Real Madrid youth team, and even managed to score.

243
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:15,490
You're amazing, brother!

244
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,810
...There are people in the world far more amazing than me.

245
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,380
What are you saying all of a sudden...?

246
00:16:28,990 --> 00:16:31,090
...I've changed my dream!

247
00:16:31,910 --> 00:16:34,880
I'm going to become the best midfielder in the world!

248
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:39,160
Don't you mean the best striker?

249
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:42,980
...There's no meaning in becoming the best midfielder in the wor-

250
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:43,960
Shut up.

251
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,360
...Your words are those of someone who knows nothing about the world.

252
00:16:47,810 --> 00:16:49,320
What nonsense is this...?

253
00:16:49,710 --> 00:16:53,570
Didn't you say we'd fight together...?! Didn't you tell me to become the best after you?

254
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:59,370
...I did. That's why I'll become the best midfielder in the world, and you'll become the best striker in the world.

255
00:16:59,370 --> 00:17:02,330
Me...! The younger brother of the world's best striker!

256
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:08,190
Did you come back just to say such pitiful things?!

257
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:10,750
...I don't want to see you like this!

258
00:17:11,630 --> 00:17:12,390
...You...

259
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:16,330
You're not the brother I shared the same dream with!!

260
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:22,820
...I understand now.

261
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,170
...How pitiful we are.

262
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:30,440
...You... and me.

263
00:17:31,830 --> 00:17:33,370
What do you mean?

264
00:17:34,690 --> 00:17:40,080
If you can defeat me in this one-on-one duel... then I'll share the same dream with you again!

265
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:45,360
But if I win... this is the end of our dream right here.

266
00:17:46,330 --> 00:17:49,670
I don't want this...! Don't decide something like that on your own, brother!

267
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:52,230
...I don't want to have a duel like this!

268
00:17:52,930 --> 00:17:54,670
Here I come... Rin!

269
00:17:58,190 --> 00:18:00,100
First to score wins!

270
00:18:02,970 --> 00:18:03,850
How fast!

271
00:18:05,270 --> 00:18:07,370
...His level is higher than when he was in Japan!

272
00:18:07,850 --> 00:18:10,010
But I won't let him pass anymore!

273
00:18:19,450 --> 00:18:23,160
...So this is my brother's current level.

274
00:18:24,930 --> 00:18:25,810
Why...?

275
00:18:27,070 --> 00:18:28,020
Brother!

276
00:18:29,930 --> 00:18:33,230
...Rin... for the four years I was away...

277
00:18:39,110 --> 00:18:42,800
...what the hell were you doing here?

278
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,570
It's over.

279
00:18:58,150 --> 00:18:59,660
...Wait, brother!

280
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:04,740
...I worked so hard while you were gone!

281
00:19:05,070 --> 00:19:09,180
...I worked so hard to become the best in Japan and attract the attention of scouts like you!

282
00:19:10,010 --> 00:19:11,980
...I tried to become your replacement!

283
00:19:12,510 --> 00:19:17,770
...And I fought for the team until I became the best in Japan, just like I promised you!

284
00:19:18,130 --> 00:19:20,850
After all that, does it end this easily...?

285
00:19:22,450 --> 00:19:25,610
...If we don't pursue our dream together, then I...

286
00:19:27,260 --> 00:19:30,200
...have no reason to play football anymore.

287
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:35,370
Then quit.

288
00:19:41,170 --> 00:19:43,180
...The best in Japan, he says.

289
00:19:43,910 --> 00:19:46,120
...Replace me, he says.

290
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:50,410
...You make me want to vomit!

291
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:54,830
...Don't make me the reason you play football again!

292
00:19:55,660 --> 00:20:00,470
...Because to me... you've just become an annoying, eyesore of a brother!

293
00:20:01,430 --> 00:20:04,180
...You have no value to me anymore!

294
00:20:05,610 --> 00:20:06,880
...Get lost, Rin.

295
00:20:07,670 --> 00:20:10,850
...Because I don't need you in my life anymore.

296
00:20:12,410 --> 00:20:13,520
...Brother.

297
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:21,950
...I've had enough of football.

298
00:20:22,490 --> 00:20:26,580
...I only played from the beginning just to be by my brother's side.

299
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:33,600
...But in his eyes, I was nothing more than a stepping stone for him to become the best in the world.

300
00:20:34,730 --> 00:20:38,280
...And now that I have no value to him... I'm unnecessary to him.

301
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:41,340
...My older brother, who I looked up to...

302
00:20:43,210 --> 00:20:45,660
...all this time... was just a lie.

303
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:49,470
We'll both become the best in the world!

304
00:21:01,450 --> 00:21:03,660
...No... no!

305
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:05,490
No, no, no!

306
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:09,410
...These feelings... and those times we spent together...

307
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:12,300
...aren't things I can just ignore and act like they never happened!

308
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:15,370
...Because they weren't a lie!

309
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:20,210
I'll kill him...! I'll never forgive him for what he did!

310
00:21:24,890 --> 00:21:25,810
Rin.

311
00:21:26,470 --> 00:21:27,840
The second half is about to start.

312
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:28,970
Got it.

313
00:21:31,850 --> 00:21:34,280
...To destroy Itoshi's dream...

314
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:36,840
...I kept playing football.

315
00:21:43,030 --> 00:21:44,020
...How annoying.

316
00:21:44,590 --> 00:21:48,290
...As expected, they put that antenna bastard in.

317
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:53,410
How will we deal with this, Ego-san?

318
00:21:53,410 --> 00:21:55,880
We won't change anything in our formation.

319
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:59,500
They've already practiced how to deal with Shidou Ryusei.

320
00:21:59,810 --> 00:22:02,250
...He can't do much alone anyway.

321
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:06,220
And of course, that figurehead coach won't be able to use him effectively.

322
00:22:06,460 --> 00:22:08,180
...What interests me more is...

323
00:22:08,620 --> 00:22:13,140
...why Itoshi Sae wants Shidou Ryusei, whom even we couldn't tame.

324
00:22:14,010 --> 00:22:17,850
...I want to see Itoshi Sae's definition of egoism.

325
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:22,210
...This is... the real beginning of the match!

326
00:23:49,590 --> 00:23:52,620
Blue Lock: Additional Time!

327
00:23:53,930 --> 00:23:55,770
...My brother's principles.

328
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,540
I'm off!

329
00:23:58,430 --> 00:24:01,910
My older brother always puts on his left shoe first.

330
00:24:02,190 --> 00:24:04,420
Aren't you supposed to say "take care," Rin?

331
00:24:05,130 --> 00:24:07,090
Take care!

332
00:24:07,510 --> 00:24:12,430
My older brother starts eating curry and rice from the middle.

333
00:24:12,670 --> 00:24:13,870
Look, Rin!

334
00:24:13,870 --> 00:24:17,470
This is the Battle of Sekigahara in curry and rice. It tastes better here.

335
00:24:17,470 --> 00:24:19,310
...How delicious Sekigahara is!

336
00:24:20,810 --> 00:24:22,130
On rainy days,

337
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:25,950
...he scribbles on the sunshine doll with his fingernails.

338
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:29,220
Make it sunny, you stupid doll!

339
00:24:29,220 --> 00:24:32,090
I can't play football like this!

340
00:24:32,090 --> 00:24:34,860
Make it sunny, rain doll!

341
00:24:39,670 --> 00:24:41,150
...When the rainbow appears,

342
00:24:42,270 --> 00:24:43,820
...he plays with me.

343
00:24:43,820 --> 00:24:45,450
No, not like that, Rin.

344
00:24:45,450 --> 00:24:46,890
A little more to the right.

345
00:24:46,890 --> 00:24:49,180
Down... right there! Stop!

346
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:50,170
Here I come.

347
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,240
...Gross.

348
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:55,800
...It's literally trash.

349
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:59,850
...Trash! Trash! Literally trash!

350
00:25:01,770 --> 00:25:03,600
Ah, you! Be careful, Rin!

351
00:25:04,060 --> 00:25:05,280
Watch where you're stepping.

352
00:25:06,600 --> 00:25:07,490
...Okay.

353
00:25:11,190 --> 00:25:12,860
...You son of a bitch.

354
00:25:14,740 --> 00:25:17,110
Hey, you little rascal!!!

355
00:25:17,110 --> 00:25:18,340
...Amazing!

356
00:25:18,340 --> 00:25:19,530
Let's run, Rin!

357
00:25:22,070 --> 00:25:24,120
We'll be dead if we get caught!

358
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:27,990
Wait, you rascals! That was dangerous!

359
00:25:27,990 --> 00:25:31,970
Shut up! In your dreams, you senile old driver!

360
00:25:31,970 --> 00:25:33,750
Senile old driver!!

361
00:25:34,750 --> 00:25:35,800
Come on! Run!

362
00:25:36,490 --> 00:25:38,410
...Playing with my brother...

363
00:25:39,700 --> 00:25:40,630
Okay!

364
00:25:40,870 --> 00:25:43,180
...is always fun.